  "notes": "The one prayer of the Canon said aloud, and the one at which the priest strikes his breast — the two go together: the raised voice is the rubric's own elata aliquantulum voce. Its list of saints answers the list in Communicántes: John the Baptist, Stephen, Matthias, Barnabas, Ignatius, Alexander, Marcellinus, Peter, then seven women — Felicity, Perpetua, Agatha, Lucy, Agnes, Cecilia, Anastasia. ÆSTIMÁTOR at w048 and LARGÍTOR at w053 are vocative, addressed to God as the imperative admítte is, on the corpus's ruling at ordinarium.in-spiritu-humilitatis w027; the nominative is the competing reading, and the two forms are identical. ÁLIQUAM at w012 is tagged pronoun with both analyzers. PERPÉTUA at w033 is the martyr's name; Whitaker's Words knows only the adjective perpétuus and contradicts the reading, which the agreement report records.",
